<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    GELATINOUSSLIME_GAPPO_FAMILY_1: the filter-feeder line of the Slime ("a whole family of
    scooping-mouthed animals grazing the Slime itself", owner). One stem, three sizes (the oomb
    precedent): lesser gappo (skimming swarm), gappo (the middle size, the old campaign slime grazer
    moved here with its v2 art; the campaign def is deleted), greater gappo (slow bulk feeder; its scoop leaves a clean channel,
    RM_CompGappoChannel, gated by SlimeSettings.gappoChannels).
    Resistant by identity (filter-feeders on the body): RM_SlimeResistant extension. Never hostile.
    One home: the Slime only (wired inline on RM_GelatinousSlime/wildAnimals). No member flies.
    All numbers are // INVENTED. Art: gappo = artpipe rutslimegrazer_v2; lesser and greater from
    art_lists/gelatinousslime_turn1_2026-10-02.csv, all three facings wired.
  -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_GappoLesser</defName>
    <label>lesser gappo</label>
    <description>A knee-high skimmer with a shovel-lipped scoop, pale amber and smooth as a wet pebble. Lesser gappos move in fast, shifting swarms across the body's surface, sieving the film off the top in long shallow passes. The Slime does not seem to notice the grazing.</description>
